  "body": "## Problem\n\nThe quick gate compares the worktree against the local `main` branch. In this repository, agents do not pull in the main checkout while a gate runs (#1201). Thus the local `main` can be many commits behind `origin/main`.\n\nWhen the base is stale, the diff holds many files that the branch did not change. The quick gate then falls back to the batch plan.\n\n## Seen\n\nOn the branch of PR #3738, the local `main` was `d66400b78`. The diff against it had 2056 files. The quick gate fell back to batch. The change itself touched only `xtask/`.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe quick gate uses the merge base with `origin/main` (after `git fetch`), or it warns when the local `main` is behind `origin/main`.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `gate heavy --base main` can have the same problem.\n- A test must pin the choice of the base.\n",
